{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__General_Awareness__General_Studies__Super_Practice__General_Awareness_-_General_Studies_-_Super_Practice_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_72_(20Q)","path":"organized/Others/General Awareness/General Studies/Super Practice/General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 72 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/General Awareness/General Studies/Super Practice","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the length and the breadth of a rectangle are increased by 15% and 20%, respectively, then by how much percent the area of the rectangle will increase?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;: 15% &#2324;&#2352; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">32%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">38%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">38%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48%</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let length and width of a rectangle is 10x and 10y respectively.</p><p>Initial area = 10x * 10y = 100xy</p><p>New length = 115% of 10x = 11.5x</p><p>New width = 120% of 10y = 12y</p><p>New area = 11.5x * 12y = 138xy</p><p>Required percent increment = <img border=0 width=143 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21022/image055.png\"></p><p>= 38%</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The side of a square is 5 cm. If the side is doubled, by how many times will the area of the square increase?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 5 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Side of a square = 5 cm</p><p>Area of the square = 5*5 = 25 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>If the side is doubled, then Side of a square = 2 * 5 =10 cm</p><p>Area of the square = 10*10 = 100 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of the square increases by = 100 /25 = 4 times</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The lengths of the two diagonals of a rhombus are 20 cm and 23 cm. What is the area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the rhombus? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 23 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">460</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">460</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">345</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">345</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">230</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">230</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">115</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">115</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>We know that:-</p><p>Area of rhombus = (1/2)  X  d<sub>1</sub>  X  d<sub>2</sub>. </p><p>d<sub>1</sub> = 20 cm, d<sub>2</sub> = 23 cm. </p><p>Area = (1/2)  X  20  X  23 = 460 / 2 = 230 cm<sup>2</sup>. </p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A rectangle with perimeter 50 cm has its sides in the ratio 1 : 4. What is the perimeter of a square whose area is the same as that of the rectangle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>50 cm &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 1 : 4 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">45 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let l = 4m and b = m</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 50 cm</p><p>2(4m + m) = 50</p><p>m = 5</p><p>l = 20cm and b = 5cm</p><p>Area of the rectangle = area of the square</p><p>Area of the square = 20 * 5 =100 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Side of the square = &radic;100 = 10cm</p><p>Perimeter of the square = 4 * 10 = 40 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a parallelogram with base 26 cm and height 18 cm is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">234 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">234 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">936 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">936 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">932 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">932 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">468 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">468 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Base=26 cm</p><p>Height= 18 cm</p><p>Area of parallelogram= base*height</p><p>Area=26*18 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>=468 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a rectangular field is 396 m&#178;, whose sides are in the ratio of 11:9. What is the perimeter of the rectangular field?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 396 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 11:9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">76 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">76 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">80 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">80 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">78 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">78 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">74 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">74 &#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let sides be 11k and 9k.</p><p>Area = 11k  X  9k = 99k&#178; = 396,</p><p>so k&#178; = 4,</p><p>k = 2.</p><p>Sides = 22 m and 18 m.</p><p>Perimeter = 2(22 + 18) = <b>80 m</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The length of two parallel sides of a trapezium are <i>25 </i>metre and 30 metre. If its height is 20 metres, then what is the area of the trapezium?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 25 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 30 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 20 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">420 metre<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">420 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">350 metre<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">350 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">590 metre<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">590 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">550 metre<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">550 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Area of trapezium = (1/2) * (a + b) * h</p><p>Where 'a' and 'b' is the length of parallel sides of the trapezium and 'h' is the perpendicular distance between those two parallel sides.</p><p>Area of given trapezium = (1/2) * (25 + 30) * 20</p><p>= 55 * 10</p><p>= 550 metre<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>One diagonal of a rhombus is 8&radic;3. If the other diagonal is equal to its side, then the area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the rhombus is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; 8&radic;3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">16&radic;3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16&radic;3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12&radic;3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12&radic;3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32&radic;3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32&radic;3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24&radic;3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24&radic;3</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img width=250 height=227 id=\"Picture 33\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image056.png\"></p><p>By Pythagoras theorem,</p><p><img width=83 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image057.png\"></p><p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image058.png\"></p><p><img width=52 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image059.png\"></p><p><img width=36 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20419/image060.png\"></p><p>Area of the rhombus = (1/2) * 8 * 8&radic;3 = 32&radic;3 sq. cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sum of the squares of the sides of a rhombus is 1600cm<sup>2</sup>. What is the side of the rhombus?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; 1600 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Since the sides of the rhombus are equal.</p><p>4a<sup>2</sup> = 1600</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 400</p><p>a = 20cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the perimeter of a certain rectangle is 50 units and its area is 150 sq. units, then how many units is the length of its shorter side?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 50 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 150 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Perimeter of the rectangle = 2(l + b)</p><p>2 (l + b) = 50</p><p>(l + b) = 50/2</p><p>(l + b) = 25</p><p>Put b = 10 and l = 15, then condition satisfied.</p><p>Area of the rectangle = l * b = 15* 10 = 150 (satisfied)</p><p>Required answer = 10 units.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a rectangular field, the sum of the length and the breadth is 9 cm and area is 18 cm<sup>2</sup>. If the length is 'a' and breadth is 'b', then find the value of (a<sup>2</sup> &#8722; ab + b<sup>2</sup>).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;<sup>2</sup>&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 'a' &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 'b' &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (a<sup>2</sup> &#8722; ab + b<sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Sum of length and breadth:</p><p>a + b = 9</p><p>Area of the rectangle:</p><p>a  X  b = 18</p><p>We can rewrite a<sup>2</sup>  -  ab + b<sup>2</sup> as (a + b)<sup>2</sup>  -  3ab</p><p>Now, substitute these values into the equation:</p><p>=&gt; a&#178; - ab + b&#178; = (9)&#178; - 3  X  18</p><p>=&gt; 81  -  54 = 27</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A rectangular courtyard is 4m 95cm long and 16m 65cm broad. It is to be paved with the square tiles of the same size. Find the least number of such square tiles required to pave the rectangular courtyard.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2310;&#2306;&#2327;&#2344; 4 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; 95 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 16 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; 65 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2310;&#2306;&#2327;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2320;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">877</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">877</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">944</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">944</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">388</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">388</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">407</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">407</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>We are given a rectangular courtyard with dimensions:</p><p>&#183; Length = 4&#8201;m&#8201;95&#8201;cm</p><p>&#183; Breadth = 16&#8201;m&#8201;65&#8201;cm</p><p>&#183; We need to find the least number of square tiles required to completely pave the rectangular courtyard.</p><p><b>Step 1: Convert the dimensions to a consistent unit (centimeters)</b></p><p>&#183; Length = 4&#8201;m&#8201;95&#8201;cm=495&#8201;cm (since 1 meter = 100 cm)</p><p>&#183; Breadth = 16&#8201;m&#8201;65&#8201;cm=1665&#8201;cm</p><p><b>Step 2: Find the side length of the largest square tile</b></p><p>The side length of the largest square tile that can tile the courtyard exactly will be the <b>greatest common divisor (GCD)</b> of the length and breadth of the courtyard, because the GCD represents the largest possible side length that can divide both dimensions without leaving a remainder.</p><p>Now, find the GCD of 495&#8201;cm and 1665&#8201;cm</p><p><b>Using the Euclidean algorithm to find the GCD:</b></p><p>1665&div;495&#8776;3(quotient)1665 </p><p>1665&#8722;3 X 495=1665&#8722;1485=180</p><p>495&div;180&#8776;2(quotient)</p><p>495&#8722;2 X 180=495&#8722;360=135 </p><p>180&div;135&#8776;1(quotient)180</p><p>180&#8722;1 X 135=180&#8722;135=45</p><p>135&div;45=3(quotient) </p><p>Since the remainder is now 0, the GCD is 45 cm.</p><p><b>Step 3: Find the area of the courtyard</b></p><p>The area of the courtyard is:</p><p>Area of the courtyard=495&#8201;cm X 1665&#8201;cm=823,575&#8201;cm<sup>2</sup> </p><p><b>Step 4: Find the area of one square tile</b></p><p>The area of one square tile with side length 45 cm is:</p><p>Area of one square tile=45&#8201;cm X 45&#8201;cm=2025&#8201;cm<sup>2</sup> </p><p><b>Step 5: Find the number of tiles required</b></p><p>To find the number of tiles required, divide the area of the courtyard by the area of one square tile:</p><p>Number of tiles=Area of the courtyard/Area of one square tile=823,575/2025=407 </p><p><b>Step 6: Conclusion</b></p><p>Thus, the least number of square tiles required to pave the courtyard is <b>407</b>.</p><p>The correct answer is <b>d) 407</b>.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a square is 16x<sup>2 </sup>+40x +25 square units.Find the perimeter of the square.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 16x<sup>2 </sup>+40x +25 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3(10x+8)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3(10x+8)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3(8x+10)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3(8x+10)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2(10x+8)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2(10x+8)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2(8x+10)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2(8x+10)</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>16x<sup>2 </sup>+40x +25 it can be written as (4x+5)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>And we know area of a square=side<sup>2</sup> </p><p>So side<sup>2</sup>=(4x+5)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Side=(4x+5)</p><p>Perimeter=4*side=4*(4x+5)=2*(8x+10)</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a square shaped field is 1764 m<sup>2</sup>. The breadth of a rectangular park is 1/3<sup>rd </sup>of the side of the square field and its length is two times its breadth. What is the cost (in &#8377;) of levelling the park at &#8377;15 per m<sup>2</sup>?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2326;&#2375;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 1764 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2326;&#2375;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; 1/3 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8377;15 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; m<sup>2 </sup>&#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">4290</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4290</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4200</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5880</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5880</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4320</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4320</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Area of square field = 1764</p><p>Side of square field = &radic;1764 = 42 m</p><p>Breadth of rectangular park = 42 * 1/3 = 14 m</p><p>Length of rectangular park = 14 * 2 = 28 m</p><p>Area of rectangular park = 14 * 28 = 392 sq.m</p><p>Cost of levelling park at Rs.15 per sq. m = 15 * 392 = Rs.5880</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A wire is in the form of square with side 44 cm. It is bent to form a circle. What is the radius of the circle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; 44 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2350;&#2379;&#2396;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">28 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">21 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Since the wire of same length is bent from square to circle. Which means the perimeter of square will be equal to the circumference of circle.</p><p>Perimeter of square = Circumference of circle</p><p>4 * 44 = 2&#960;R</p><p>R = 28 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of the top of a rectangular table is 56 meter and its area is 192 meter<sup>2</sup>, what is the length of its diagonal?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 56 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 192 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;, &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">22 meter</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 meter</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 meter</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18 meter</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the length and width of the top of rectangular table is 'l' m and 'b' m respectively.</p><p>Perimeter of table = 2(l + b) = 56</p><p>L + b = 28 ........ (1)</p><p>Area of table = lb = 192 ...... (2)</p><p>(l + b)<sup>2</sup> = l<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + 2lb</p><p>28<sup>2</sup> = l<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + 2 * 192</p><p>L<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2 </sup>= 784  -  384 = 400</p><p>Length of diagonal of the table = &radic;(l<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;400</p><p>= 20 meter</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a rectangle is 50 cm. Its area and length are in the ratio of 5 : 1. Find the length of the rectangle .</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 50 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 5 : 1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let area and length of the rectangle are 5m and m respectively.</p><p>Breadth of the rectangle = 5m/m = 5 cm</p><p>Perimeter of a rectangle = 50 cm</p><p>2 (m + 5) = 50</p><p>m + 5 = 25</p><p>m = 20 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the length of a certain rectangle is decreased by 4 cm and breadth is increased by 2 cm, it would result in a square of the same area. What is the perimeter of the original rectangle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 4 cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2 cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let length and width of the rectangle is 'l' cm and 'b' cm respectively.</p><p>Side of square = l  -  4 = b + 2</p><p>l = b + 6 ......... (1)</p><p>Area of rectangle = Area of square</p><p>lb = (l  -  4) (b + 2)</p><p>lb = lb + 2l  -  4b  -  8</p><p>l = 2b + 4 ......... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>b + 6 = 2b + 4</p><p>b = 2 and l = 8</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 2 (l + b) = 2 (8 + 2)</p><p>= 20 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of a square whose diagonal is of 14 cm length.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">95 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">95 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">98 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">98 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">94 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">94 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">96 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">96 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Diagonal of square = 14 cm</p><p>Side of square = 14/&radic;2 cm</p><p>Area of square = (14/&radic;2)<sup>2</sup> = 98 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a rectangular garden is 48 m. If the length is 6 m more than the breadth, the area (in m<sup>2</sup>) of the garden is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 48 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">135</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">135</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">96</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">96</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">84</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">84</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">112</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">112</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let Breadth be B.</p><p>Then, Length L = B + 6</p><p>Perimeter = 2(L + B)</p><p>48 = 2(B + 6 + B)</p><p>48 = 2(2B + 6)</p><p>48 = 4B + 12</p><p>=&gt; 4B = 48 - 12</p><p>=&gt; 4B = 36</p><p>=&gt; B = 36 / 4</p><p>=&gt; B = 9</p><p>Length L = B + 6</p><p>=&gt; 9 + 6 = 15</p><p>Area = L  X  B</p><p>=&gt; 15  X  9 = 135 m<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}